n past sell-offs it fell 57% in the 2020 crash, 46% in the 2022 bear market and 81% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $17.88 (margin of safety -108%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 54%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $11.36 to $29.35 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Technology peers: P/E 90.7 vs 26.7, EV/EBITDA 32.3 vs 16.4 and P/FCF 42.7 vs 25.4 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 98% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 2.3% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.0% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $61.33 on average, 65% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 12% earns above the cost of capital of 10.5%, but the 1pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar.","It runs a 40% gross margin and converts 8% of revenue into free cash flow, or 2% after stock compensation.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.96x.","ROE of 4% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.5x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 14pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 18.0% of revenue on R&D and 5.6% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $164.2M.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.8, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 4.75).","Working capital ties up about 262 days of sales, a drag on cash generation."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 0.9% over 3 years, 7.9% over 5 years and 3.4% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 25%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 11.7% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 8.0% a year over five years.","Margins are contracting (-1.6% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.97, a backlog worth 6% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 14%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.8x, 2.4% of sales), a maintenance pace."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.2%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (19 sales, net $27.0M sold).","The share count has grown 3.8% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 15.4% of the float, 8.3 days to cover."],"people":["With about 1,265 employees, each generates about $525K of revenue, 1.4x the Technology median, and productivity has fallen 2.7% a year.","That works out to $42K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $694K (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $29K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":48,"head":"Avoid: priced 108% above its fair value of $17.88.","pros":["Revenue grew 7.9%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $164.2M","Altman Z in the safe zone","3 analysts' mean target $61.33 (+65%)","12-1 month momentum +91%"],"cons":["Trades 108% above fair value of $17.88","P/E 90.7x vs sector 26.7x","EV/EBITDA 32.3x vs sector 16.4x","P/FCF 42.7x vs sector 25.4x","Heavy insider selling ($27.0M net over 12 months)"],"flags":["Priced 108% above its fair value of $17.88"],"need":[],"buy_below":15.2,"vc":{"base":17.88,"base_src":"dcf","bear":11.36,"bull":29.35,"alt_median":5.35,"n_alt":1,"gap":2.3431,"dispersion":0.5395,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (54% dispersion)","DCF is 234% above the other models' median ($5.35)"]},"med":{"pe":26.7484,"ev_ebitda":16.351,"pfcf":25.4376,"pb":3.7763,"roic":0.0752,"gross_margin":0.4714,"fcf_margin":0.1275,"div_yield":0.0129}},"ticker":"VECO","date":"2026-11-06"}